We want the prob. That the smaller number among the two is less than 4
$$\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{P}(\text { smaller }<4) & =1-\mathrm{P}(\text { smaller } \geq 4) \\
& =1-\frac{6}{30}=\frac{4}{5}
\end{aligned}$$

Given quadratic equation has equal roots, thus
$$\begin{array}{l}
D=0 \Rightarrow\left(f^{\prime}(x)\right)^{2}=f^{\prime \prime}(x) \cdot f(x) \\
\frac{f^{\prime}(x)}{f(x)}=\frac{f^{\prime \prime}(x)}{f^{\prime}(x)}
\end{array}$$

Required energy to be supplied $=\Delta \mathrm{E}=\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{f}}-\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{i}}$
$$\begin{aligned}
\Delta E & =\left(\frac{-G M_{E} m}{2\left(3 R_{E}\right)}\right)-\left(\frac{-G M_{E} m}{2\left(1.5 R_{E}\right)}\right) \\
& =\frac{G M_{E} m}{6 R_{E}}
\end{aligned}$$

$\frac{1}{\lambda}=\mathrm{RZ}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\mathrm{n}_{1}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\mathrm{n}_{2}^{2}}\right)$
For Ist line of lyman series in H-atom
$$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{1}{\lambda}=\mathrm{R}(1)^{2}\left(\frac{1}{1^{2}}-\frac{1}{2^{2}}\right) \\
\frac{1}{\lambda}=\frac{3 \mathrm{R}}{4}
\end{array}$$
for $2^{\text {nd }}$ line of Balmer series of $\mathrm{He}^{+}$
$$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{1}{\lambda^{\prime}}=\mathrm{R}(2)^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2^{2}}-\frac{1}{4^{2}}\right) \\
\frac{1}{\lambda^{\prime}}=\frac{3 \mathrm{R}}{4}
\end{array}$$
